+# Carbon Gate Policy & Override Process
+
+Purpose
+- Provide documented tuning and operator override procedures for the Aegis carbon gate to avoid blocking critical operations while still reducing emissions.
+
+Policy summary
+- Monitor mode must run for at least 14 days (collect rolling mean, median, variance).
+- Compute suggested threshold = baseline (org target) * (1 + variance_factor). Tune variance_factor to limit false positive rate to < 5% in historic data.
+- Enforce mode blocks promotions when rolling mean > threshold, unless a valid override artifact is presented.
+
+Override artifact requirements
+- Format: JSON following ops/governance/approval_artifact_schema.json
+- Must be cosign-signed by an authorized Platform Owner KMS principal
+- Must include expiry (default TTL 60 minutes) and scope (which manifests / runs it applies to)
+- All overrides are recorded via evidence_sdk and retained in S3
+
+Operator steps to create override
+1. Compose artifact:
+   python3 ops/carbon/override_signer.py --approval-id APPROVAL-123 --approved-by alice@example.com --scope '{"manifests":"deploy.yaml"}' --out /tmp/override.json --ttl-min 60
+2. Verify signature:
+   cosign verify /tmp/override.json
+3. Re-run CI promote with override_artifact=/tmp/override.json
+
+Auditing & retention
+- Every override must be logged (ops.sdk.evidence_sdk.record_manifest) and retained for at least 365 days.
+- Monthly review of overrides by Safety Officer and Platform Owner.
+
+Tuning guidance
+- Start with Aegis_CARBON_PROMOTE_THRESHOLD_GCO2 = org target (e.g., 300 gCO2/kWh).
+- Run monitor mode for 14 days -> compute FP rate if gate enforced at candidate thresholds.
+- Choose threshold that keeps FP < 5% while achieving reduction goals.
+
